0 -14 Td
(1\) File formats and sample rates) Tj
0 -14 Td
(* Deliver WAV or FLAC \(lossless\) at 44.1 kHz or 48 kHz and 24-bit depth.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(* Include one low-bitrate preview MP3 \(128-192 kbps\) for quick auditioning in apps) Tj
0 -14 Td
(that don't need lossless files.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(2\) Loudness and mastering) Tj
0 -14 Td
(* There is no universal -14 LUFS delivery target for every streaming platform or) Tj
0 -14 Td
(clinical playback system. Check the recipient's current delivery specification rather) Tj
0 -14 Td
(than treating one loudness value as mandatory.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(* Preserve an unclipped, high-quality master. Measure and document integrated loudness) Tj
0 -14 Td
(and maximum true peak; create platform-specific versions only when a delivery) Tj
0 -14 Td
(specification calls for them.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(* LUFS describes the audio file, not the sound pressure reaching a listener. Set) Tj
0 -14 Td
(playback level according to the care team's or facility's guidance; do not use a) Tj
0 -14 Td
(mastering target to set a patient's listening volume.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(* When helpful, include an unprocessed master alongside a clearly labeled delivery) Tj
0 -14 Td
(master.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(3\) Create multiple edits) Tj
0 -14 Td
(* Full track \(3-5 minutes typical\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
